Certainly! Here's a translation of the provided text into uvl-Code:

```uvl
class CoffeeShop {
    attribute String name;
}

class Drink {
    attribute String type; // e.g., Coffee, Tea
}

class Food {
    attribute String type; // e.g., Croissant, Bagel
}

class PaymentMethod {
    attribute String method; // e.g., Card, Cash
}

class Transaction {
    attribute PaymentMethod paymentMethod;
    attribute List<Drink> drinks;
    attribute List<Food> foods;
}

association "sells" {
    class CoffeeShop;
    class Drink;
    multiplicity 1..*;
}

association "sells" {
    class CoffeeShop;
    class Food;
    multiplicity 1..*;
}

association "uses" {
    class Transaction;
    class PaymentMethod;
    multiplicity 1;
}

association "includes" {
    class Transaction;
    class Drink;
    multiplicity 0..*;
}

association "includes" {
    class Transaction;
    class Food;
    multiplicity 0..*;
}
```

This uvl-Code defines the classes and associations based on the information provided in the text. Each class represents an entity, and the associations represent the relationships between these entities.